factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 2 problems
  Slides text says the 3rd-kaalam (3ஆம்கால) yagasalai/velvi puja and the kudamuzhukku happen on Sunday, and the article says 6 am is 3rd-kaalam puja, which is consistent; however the caption's 'சனிக்கிழமை' pooja description is fine. Main issue: the reel_script states the 6 am 3rd-kaalam velvi puja 'நடைபெறும்' before the kudamuzhukku, which matches the article, but the slides_spec 'எங்கே?' line 'தமிழ் முறைப்படி குடமுழுக்கு நடைபெறும்' is placed under location, which mixes the ceremony type into the place slide.
  The reel_script omits the article's detail that the Thai-style temple ceremony is done per Tamil tradition only in the slides, not in the reel - minor, but the reel says 'வெள்ளிக்கிழமை விநாயகர், நவக்கிரக, வாஸ்து பூஜைகள்' and then says devotees took holy water 'அவர்கள்' without distinguishing; the reel also drops the 'முருக பக்தர்கள்' nuance (acceptable), and sentence 'சனிக்கிழமை முதல்கால யாகசாலை பூஜைகளும், மாலை 2ஆம்கால வேள்வி பூஜைகளும் நடைபெற்றன' states past tense for events the article describes as scheduled for Saturday, which is a tense mismatch with the source wording 'நடைபெற்றன' that is acceptable.
